he supplied grant. The grant names the author, actor://codex/root/public_preparation_worker, and the qualification.ts territory with preimage 63484B/8f92906d. This is the intermediate postimage recorded in the reference-attribution closure (63360+124=63484). The activation and closure name the same author and actor, and the preimage manifest lists 8f929/63484. The delta removes 'if (task.scope !== undefined) ' (30B) from material validation and the ungrouped ternary (42B) from the attribution rendering. That gives 63412B, which matches the closure's 0ee4bc36 entry; the current body shows both edits. Per the grant, proof.ts stays at 9b6b1ec6. The activation scope is qualification.ts only, which matches this chain. The assessor is distinct from the author. Authority is the file grant issued under the owner's 'start', mapped by grant04 to the product-owner@5 policy slot with no retroauthorization. I take this as sufficient within the trusted-desktop boundary. SHA-256 digests were not independently recomputed."}]}}}
